# ── Never ship these ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The image is published publicly (see .github/workflows/publish-image.yml), so
# anything here is world-readable. `db.sqlite3` was already excluded, but the
# entries around it were not — and a Django dumpdata is the same data in a
# different file.
#
# Found 2026-08-12: datadump.json was inside the built image carrying
# auth.user rows with password hashes and email addresses.
datadump.json
*.json.gz
db.sqlite3*
dumps/
*.dump
*.sql

